IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`
IMPORT `sca-seat`

-- State Courts Act 1970 (Singapore) -- WORKED CASES FOR THE SEAT LAYER.
-- One case at least for each question in sca-seat.l4, with the facts a real person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the Act beside the assertion, never from the code's output.
-- The District Court limit is $250,000 and the Magistrate's Court limit is $60,000 (s 2).
-- Inputs for the case questions, in order: a claim against a person; served in Singapore; served abroad; the defendant submits; a money claim; the amount claimed; the value of other relief; passing off; supervisory or review; a written law gives it to another court (My answer); section 28A affects it (My answer); the excess is given up; a signed agreement.

§ `The State Courts and the monetary limits`

#ASSERT `Is this court one of the State Courts` `District Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this court one of the State Courts` `Small Claims Tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The list in s 3(1) is not closed, so a court outside the five is not answered.
#ASSERT `Is this court one of the State Courts` `Another court or tribunal` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 19(4): "exceeds" means more than the limit.
#ASSERT `Is my claim over the District Court limit` 250_000 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim over the District Court limit` 250_001 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim over the District Court limit` 1_000 400_000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim over the Magistrate's Court limit` 60_000 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim over the Magistrate's Court limit` 60_001 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim over the Magistrate's Court limit` 1_000 70_000 EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Sittings, privacy and electronic hearings`

#ASSERT `Is the court to sit on this day` `Ordinary day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the court to sit on this day` Saturday EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the court to sit on this day` `Day in a vacation authorised under section 61` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May the court hear my case in private` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the court hear my case in private` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the court order material to be redacted` `The name, address or photograph of a witness` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the court order material to be redacted` `The name, address or photograph of a witness` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the court order material to be redacted` `Other material` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for acting against the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for acting against the order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I be present while my case is heard in private` TRUE `A journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I be present while my case is heard in private` TRUE `Anyone else` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May the court hear my case by this means` FALSE `A live video link` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the court hear my case by this means` FALSE `Another electronic means of communication not approved by the Chief Justice` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Oral evidence in a civil proceeding by audio only: not without the parties' consent.
#ASSERT `May the court hear my oral evidence by audio only` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the court hear my oral evidence by audio only` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May the court hear my oral evidence by audio only` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the court hear my oral evidence by audio only` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Which court can hear my case`

-- A contractor claims $100,000, the defendant was served in Singapore.
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same claim at $300,000: over the limit and nothing else has happened.
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 300_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The claimant gives up the excess (s 22).
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 300_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The parties sign an agreement (s 23).
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 300_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The defendant was not served and does not submit: s 19(2) "where" is not met.
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The defendant submits: s 19(2)(b).
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Passing off is outside a District Court's jurisdiction: s 19(3)(ca).
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100_000 0 TRUE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A written law vests the case exclusively elsewhere: s 19(3)(c).
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100_000 0 FALSE FALSE Yes No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Section 28A of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 affects a case in an excluded class: not decided.
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100_000 0 TRUE FALSE No Yes FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not an action in personam: s 19(2) is for actions in personam, so the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The person is not sure whether a written law gives the case elsewhere: this layer does not answer.
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100_000 0 FALSE FALSE `I am not sure` No FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- A Magistrate's Court: $60,000 and no more.
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 60_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 60_001 0 FALSE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Over the limit but the excess is given up: ss 22 and 23 name a District Court, so the Act does not answer for a Magistrate's Court (fork F-S52-2).
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 60_001 0 FALSE FALSE No No TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No claim for a sum of money: s 52(1A)(a).
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Passing off: s 52(1A)(aa).
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 10_000 0 TRUE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A supervisory or judicial review case: the limitations of a District Court apply (s 52(2), s 19(3)).
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 10_000 0 FALSE TRUE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The defendant was not served and does not submit.
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 10_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have jurisdiction over my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 10_000 0 FALSE FALSE No `I am not sure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Is my case of a kind a District Court cannot hear?  Inputs: passing off; supervisory or review; written law.
#ASSERT `Is my case of a kind a District Court cannot hear` FALSE FALSE No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my case of a kind a District Court cannot hear` TRUE FALSE No EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my case of a kind a District Court cannot hear` FALSE TRUE No EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my case of a kind a District Court cannot hear` FALSE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my case of a kind a District Court cannot hear` FALSE FALSE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING

-- May I give up the excess?  Inputs: against a person; served in Singapore; served abroad; submits; amount; value; passing off; supervisory; written law; 28A.
#ASSERT `May I give up the excess` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 300_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I give up the excess` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 250_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I give up the excess` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 100_000 400_000 FALSE FALSE No No EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A District Court would not have jurisdiction even without the excess (passing off).
#ASSERT `May I give up the excess` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 300_000 0 TRUE FALSE No No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I give up the excess` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 300_000 0 FALSE FALSE No No EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Having given up the excess: against; SG; abroad; submits; passing; supervisory; written; 28A; amount claimed; amount sought.
#ASSERT `May I still recover more than the limit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE No No 300_000 300_000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I still recover more than the limit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE No No 300_000 250_000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I still obtain relief above the limit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE No No 100_000 300_000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I still obtain relief above the limit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE No No 300_000 250_000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the judgment discharge all my demands` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the judgment discharge all my demands` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can we agree to give a District Court jurisdiction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can we agree to give a District Court jurisdiction` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Recovery of immovable property: is a recovery action; annual value; annual rent; monthly rent; last transacted price (0 = not known).
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my recovery action` TRUE 250_000 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my recovery action` TRUE 250_001 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my recovery action` TRUE 0 0 20_833 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my recovery action` TRUE 0 0 20_834 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my recovery action` TRUE 0 0 0 2_500_000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my recovery action` TRUE 0 0 0 2_500_001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my recovery action` FALSE 100 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- An equity proceeding: its kind; the amount or value; a registered limited liability partnership.
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my equity proceeding` `Execution of a trust, or a declaration that a trust subsists` 250_000 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my equity proceeding` `Execution of a trust, or a declaration that a trust subsists` 250_001 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my equity proceeding` `Dissolution or winding up of a partnership` 100_000 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my equity proceeding` `Dissolution or winding up of a partnership` 100_000 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my equity proceeding` `Another kind of proceeding` 100 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my distress action` 250_000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction over my distress action` 250_001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Interpleader: a bailiff's execution; adverse claims; the amount or value.
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction to grant me interpleader relief` TRUE TRUE 250_000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction to grant me interpleader relief` TRUE TRUE 250_001 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction to grant me interpleader relief` TRUE FALSE 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction to grant me interpleader relief` FALSE TRUE 100_000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction to grant me interpleader relief` FALSE TRUE 80_000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction to grant me interpleader relief` FALSE TRUE 250_000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction to grant me interpleader relief` FALSE TRUE 250_001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have jurisdiction to grant me interpleader relief` FALSE FALSE 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the High Court transfer my interpleader proceedings` TRUE 250_000 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the High Court transfer my interpleader proceedings` TRUE 250_001 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `What the court can do in my case`

#ASSERT `Does a District Court have this power` TRUE `Grant any relief, redress or remedy, or combination of remedies, absolute or conditional` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have this power` TRUE `Grant an injunction` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have this power` TRUE `Make a binding declaration of rights` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have this power` TRUE `Order the medical examination of a party` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have this power` TRUE `Order the medical examination of a party` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have this power` FALSE `Grant an injunction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does a District Court have this power` TRUE `Another power` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have this power` TRUE `Grant an injunction` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have this power` TRUE `Make an order or exercise an authority which a Judge in chambers in the General Division of the High Court could make or exercise` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have this power` TRUE `Exercise a power that section 43 or 49A gives a District Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have this power` TRUE `Order the medical examination of a party` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a Magistrate's Court have this power` FALSE `Grant an injunction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May the District Judge summon assessors` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the District Judge summon assessors` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Are the assessors' fees costs in my proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the assessors' fees costs in my proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are the assessors paid out of moneys provided by Parliament` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the assessors paid out of moneys provided by Parliament` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I object to a proposed assessor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I object to a proposed assessor` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I object to a proposed assessor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I divide my cause of action` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I divide my cause of action` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I have witnesses abroad examined` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I have witnesses abroad examined` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Costs when I sue in the High Court`

-- Could have sued in a State Court; the limit; the sum recovered; the limit lifted by s 39(4) or (5).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to more costs than a State Court would give` TRUE `The District Court limit` 250_000 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to more costs than a State Court would give` TRUE `The Magistrate's Court limit` 60_000 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to more costs than a State Court would give` TRUE `The Magistrate's Court limit` 60_001 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to more costs than a State Court would give` TRUE `The District Court limit` 100 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to more costs than a State Court would give` FALSE `The District Court limit` 100 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May the High Court allow costs on either scale` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the High Court allow costs on either scale` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Judgments, instalments and enforcement`

#ASSERT `Is the District Court's civil judgment final and conclusive` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the District Court's civil judgment final and conclusive` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the District Court's civil judgment final and conclusive` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May the District Court order payment by instalments` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the District Court order payment by instalments` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the District Court suspend or stay the judgment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the District Court suspend or stay the judgment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Instalments are ordered and there is no permission: enforcement may not issue.
#ASSERT `May enforcement issue where instalments are ordered` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May enforcement issue where instalments are ordered` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Appeals`

#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the District Court's civil decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the District Court's civil decision` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the District Court's civil decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `When may we agree the decision is final` `Before the decision was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `When may we agree the decision is final` `After the decision was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `When may we agree the decision is final` `At another time` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my appeal stop enforcement` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my appeal stop enforcement` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May the District Court decide without oral arguments` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the District Court decide without oral arguments` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May the part with oral evidence be without an oral hearing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the part with oral evidence be without an oral hearing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May the District Court hear my matter by written correspondence if unfair` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the District Court hear my matter by written correspondence if unfair` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Magistrate's Court's judgment have the same effect` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Magistrate's Court's judgment have the same effect` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Magistrate's Court's civil decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Magistrate's Court's civil decision` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

